+/// Says when a page-style pager has come to rest on a page.
+///
+/// SwiftUI writes the selection as soon as a drag passes halfway, while the
+/// page is still snapping into place, and says nothing when the snap ends.
+/// Changing the set of pages during the snap leaves the pager stopped between
+/// two of them, so a caller that changes its pages in response to a swipe
+/// needs to know when it is safe to.
+internal final class PageSettleTracker: ObservableObject {
+  var onSettle: (() -> Void)?
